@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

<section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-container">
        <div class="hero-text">
            <h5 class="text-white">We obeserve what remains</h5>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-image-wrapper">
            <img src="/img/StatueVS.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Vanitas Statue, symbol of decay " />
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="side-indicator">
        <span class="side-text">Descend</span>
        <div class="side-line"></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mission">
    <div class="mission-container">
        <div class="mission-title">
            <h1>Vanitas Studios</h1>
            <p>project</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mission-projects">
            <div class="project-content">
                <h5>Game documentation</h5>
                <p>
                    Technical and conceptual documentation of Vanitas Studios' independent projects. Development chronicles, design documents, and code analysis. The structure behind the aesthetics.
                </p>
                <a class="btn mission-btn text-uppercase" asp-page="/GameDoc">Examine Archives</a>
            </div>
            <div class="project-content">
                <h5>Articles</h5>
                <p>
                    Critical observations and aesthetic dissections of the digital medium. Analytical essays on narrative fragments, atmospheric ruins, and the philosophy of play. Observing what others overlook.
                </p>
                <a class="btn mission-btn text-uppercase" asp-page="/Blog">View Observations</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="about">
    <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-body">
            <h1>The Vision</h1>
            <p>
                Vanitas Studios dwells within the shadows, stirring the heavy veil of darkness for those who wander through it. We read what has never been written.<br />

                Every environment conceals a story—an unyielding truth. It lives in the silence of a weathered wall, a chair collapsed upon the floor, the dust suspended in the air. Silence offers what words cannot; it grants the player space to metabolize what has passed, to truly grasp the narrative.<br />

                We study and apply the design of silence in our works. We craft stories without moral boundaries, reflecting only our inherent nature. There is no perfection—only the raw beauty of authenticity.<br />

                Vanitas Studios: observing time through the lens of matter.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-visual">
            <div class="square">
                <p>02/09/2025</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
